<main class="page-content">
    <section class="page-section text-section" id="why-section">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <h1>Why type faster?</h1>
            <p class="text-section__paragraph">
                Faster typing is useful when it helps you write, study and work with less effort.
                This site keeps the basics simple: browse quotes, discuss typing, and compare results.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="text-section__grid">
            <article class="card">
                <img class="card__image" src="/assets/typewriter.jpg" alt="Old keyboard"/>
                <p class="card__text">Typing has always been about speed and clarity.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <img class="card__image" src="/assets/mechanical-keyboard.webp" alt="Modern keyboard"/>
                <p class="card__text">Modern practice is easier when the interface is simple and readable.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
                <img class="card__image" src="/assets/an-image.jpg" alt="Typing practice"/>
                <p class="card__text">Quotes and forum discussions help you practice with real text.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
        <ul class="text-section__list list">
            <li class="list__item">Finish essays and notes quicker.</li>
            <li class="list__item">Make fewer mistakes under pressure.</li>
            <li class="list__item">Feel more confident in programming and writing tasks.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="page-section text-section page-section--narrow">
        <h2>How do I improve?</h2>
        <ol class="text-section__list list">
            <li class="list__item">Use all ten fingers instead of relying on a few keys you already know.</li>
            <li class="list__item">Return to the home row between words.</li>
            <li class="list__item">Train on full quotes, not only isolated words.</li>
            <li class="list__item">Raise speed only after accuracy becomes stable.</li>
        </ol>
    </section>
</main>
